<%# The stocked shelf (D-hobby-feeds §7.1): a hand-curated list of
    publisher-run feeds, shown only while there is nothing to read.

    Offered, never subscribed. Nothing here is followed at signup or in the
    FTUE, and nothing is personalized, scored, or fetched to build the list —
    every row is a checkbox somebody ticks. That is the line READER.md's
    first promise draws: the sources are the ones the user chose.

    The shelf carries a few dozen topics, so it is browsed rather than read:
    each topic is a closed <details> (no JS — the same fold the circle cards
    and the settings channels use), and what the reader sees first is a wall
    of topic names, not a wall of checkboxes. Ticking still works while the
    folds stay shut, because the inputs are in the DOM either way.

    Locals: starters (grouped by folder); optional heading. %>
<div class="space-y-3">
  <div>
    <p class="text-sm font-medium text-ink"><%= local_assigns.fetch(:heading, "Not sure where to start?") %></p>
    <p class="text-xs text-soft">
      <%= pluralize(starters.sum { |_, entries| entries.size }, "source") %> across
      <%= pluralize(starters.size, "topic") %>, each one that has been publishing for years
      and each straight from the site itself. Open a topic and tick what you want —
      nothing is followed until you do.
    </p>
  </div>

  <%= form_with url: starters_feeds_path, class: "space-y-3" do %>
    <%= hidden_field_tag :return_to, request.path %>
    <%# Columns rather than a grid: the folds are different heights once
        opened, and a grid row is as tall as its tallest cell — which is how
        a shelf grows a hole in the middle the moment somebody opens one. %>
    <div class="gap-x-6 sm:columns-2 lg:columns-3">
      <% starters.each do |folder, entries| %>
        <details class="mb-1.5 break-inside-avoid rounded-lg border border-edge px-3 py-2">
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-baseline justify-between gap-2 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">
            <span class="text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-wide text-stone-500"><%= folder %></span>
            <span class="text-xs text-soft"><%= entries.size %></span>
          </summary>
          <div class="mt-1.5">
            <% entries.each do |entry| %>
              <label class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-0.5 text-sm">
                <%= check_box_tag "urls[]", entry.url, false, id: "starter-#{entry.url.parameterize}",
                      class: "size-3.5 shrink-0 accent-primary-600" %>
                <span class="min-w-0">
                  <span class="text-ink"><%= entry.title %></span>
                  <span class="text-xs text-soft"><%= entry.host %></span>
                </span>
              </label>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </details>
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs text-soft">
      <%= check_box_tag :create_lenses, "1", true, class: "size-3.5 accent-primary-600" %>
      Make a hobby for each group I pick
    </label>

    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline gap-3">
      <%= submit_tag "Follow the ones I ticked", class: "btn btn-secondary btn-sm" %>
      <%# The same shelf with room to read it, and the copy that survives
          this block disappearing the moment a feed is followed. %>
      <%= link_to "Browse them all", explore_feeds_path, class: "reader-filter" %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
